# shubhxho — content-first site

All public copy lives in `content/` and is loaded by `src/lib/content.ts`. Prefer editing markdown over hardcoding UI strings.

## Edit here

| Need | File / folder |
|------|----------------|
| Homepage intro + section labels | `content/home.md` |
| Projects | `content/projects/*.md` |
| Blog posts | `content/blog/*.md` |
| Gallery mosaic | `content/gallery.md` |
| Timeline / history | `content/timeline.md` |
| About / contact / privacy | `content/pages/*.md` |

## Do

- Add a project → new file in `content/projects/` with `title`, `description`, `href`, `role`, `year`, `tip`, `order`
- Add a post → new `content/blog/*.md` with `title`, `description`, `date` + body
- Change gallery tiles → lines in `content/gallery.md`: `id | file | title | /p/N | feature|tall|wide|`

## Don't

- Hardcode homepage projects, posts, gallery, or timeline in components
- Import `node:fs` / `@/lib/content` into client components — use `@/lib/content-types` for types only
- Rewrite the Next.js agent block in `AGENTS.md` (Next regenerates it)

## Commands

```bash
npm run dev      # http://localhost:3000
npm run build
npm test         # build + agentic smoke tests
```

Routes: `/` `/blog` `/gallery` `/history` `/about` `/contact` `/privacy` plus `/llms.txt` `/profile.md` `/feed.xml`
